@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Exact-edge projection cache — stable read and mutation lifecycle

actor "builder / mutating analysis" as BUILDER #FFE8CC
rectangle "CodePropertyGraph\npetgraph + stable NodeId map" as CPG #DBE4FF
rectangle "first cached read\ncount · scatter · row-sort" as BUILD #FFF3BF
database "heap-owned exact-edge cache\nforward rows by layer\nreverse rows by layer\nsource rows by target" as CACHE #C3FAE8
collections "borrowed views\nCpgEdges\nCfgNeighbors\nDfgNeighbors" as VIEWS #D3F9D8
rectangle "stable consumers\nprojection · SCC · PDG · VF2\nstats and public traversal" as READERS #E5DBFF
rectangle "topology mutation\nadd node / edge\nmutable node access" as MUTATE #FFE3E3

BUILDER --> CPG : append through native adjacency
CPG --> BUILD : cache empty + read requested
BUILD --> CACHE : exact raw EdgeIndex rows
CACHE --> VIEWS : binary-partition borrowed slice
VIEWS --> READERS : deterministic, zero allocation
READERS ..> CPG : stable NodeId evidence
BUILDER --> MUTATE : next construction step
MUTATE --> CACHE : invalidate before mutation
MUTATE --> CPG : apply mutation
CPG --> CACHE : later read reuses cache

note bottom of CACHE
  Edge payloads stay in petgraph.
  Parallel edges remain distinct.
  Clone and Serde start uncached.
end note

note bottom of MUTATE
  No cached view can coexist with a
  mutable borrow in safe Rust.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#FFE8CC>| mutation owner |
  |<#DBE4FF>| authoritative CPG |
  |<#FFF3BF>| deterministic construction |
  |<#C3FAE8>| derived exact-edge index |
  |<#D3F9D8>| borrowed read views |
  |<#E5DBFF>| stable analysis consumers |
  |<#FFE3E3>| invalidation boundary |
endlegend
@enduml
